<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saga Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saga Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, with its capital at Saga. It covers the eastern part of the former Hizen province, including the lands of the Saga domain ruled by the Nabeshima until 1871. It is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arita">Arita</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imari">Imari</a> and for the Yoshinogari archaeological site of the Yayoi period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saga-prefecture.jpg" alt="Saga Prefecture" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ascesis · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nijinomatsubara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
